> This efficient tree attention kernel will be a crucial factor in tree-style speculative decoding, which we should consider prioritize.

In fact, our implementation is not based on [Dao-AILab/flash-attention](https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention), but on the [TurboMind 2.1 Attention Kernel](https://github.com/InternLM/lmdeploy/tree/main/src/turbomind/kernels/attention), which was written from scratch and its performance is about 10% better than [Dao-AILab/flash-attention](https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention).

The changes related to casual mask are roughly as follows:
```cuda
// original
    __device__ void ApplyCasualMask(FragS& frag_S, int offset_Q, int offset_K)
    {
        Impl::ForeachS(frag_S, [&](int hi, int qi, int si, int ri, float& score) {
            if (offset_Q + qi < offset_K + si) {
                score -= std::numeric_limits<float>::infinity();
            }
        });
    }
```

```cuda
// modified
    __device__ void ApplyCasualMask(
        FragS& frag_S, int offset_Q, int offset_K, const int* medusa_mask, int his_len, int input_len, int query_idx)
    {
        Impl::ForeachS(frag_S, [&](int hi, int qi, int si, int ri, float& score) {
            if (medusa_mask) {
                int rel_pos_q = offset_Q + qi - his_len;
                int rel_pos_k = offset_K + si - his_len;
                if (0 <= rel_pos_q && rel_pos_q < input_len && 0 <= rel_pos_k && rel_pos_k < input_len) {
                    if (medusa_mask[rel_pos_q * input_len + rel_pos_k] == 0) {
                        score -= std::numeric_limits<float>::infinity();
                    }
                }
                else {
                    if (offset_Q + qi < offset_K + si) {
                        score -= std::numeric_limits<float>::infinity();
                    }
                }
            }
            else {
                if (offset_Q + qi < offset_K + si) {
                    score -= std::numeric_limits<float>::infinity();
                }
            }
        });
    }
```

@cadedaniel I've refactored how the extra outputs/inputs are handled. `TensorData` is now stored in `SpecDecodeWorker` instead of `SequenceData` and the preparation is also decoupled from `_prepare_model_input` (it's done separately in `_prepare_extra_model_input`). I've also removed the CLI changes and now the information about extra inputs required by the draft model is fetched from the `ModelConfig.hf_config` e.g., for Medusa, it lives in `MedusaConfig`.

I've also added these input preparation changes as a separate PR #5101.
Please review it once you have some time. 😄
